  "chunk": "funding (“AI winter”). From Herbert Simon’s 1960 declaration that “machines\nwill be capable, within twenty years, of doing any work that a man can do”\n[32] to Marvin Minsky’s forecast that problems of creating artificial intelligence\nwould be “substantially solved” within a generation [22], the history of AI is\nmarked by predictions that have often overestimated the intelligence of AI and\nunderestimated the complexity of human intelligence.\nOne reason for these cycles is our limited understanding of the nature and\ncomplexity of intelligence itself [24]. A critical but often overlooked aspect of AI\nismetacognition— the ability to monitor and reflect on one’s own thinking pro-\ncesses [10, 27]. As Mitchell [23] argues, when humans struggle with a problem,\nthey eventually recognize that repeating ineffective strategies is futile and change\ntheir course of action accordingly. This self-awareness represents cognitive abil-",
